# Typing

Every line here is written the way Opal writes what you type, so the page shows it as typed.

## Escaped literals

Arithmetic: 2*3\*4 and 2 * 3 = 6.

A path: C:\\*.txt, and snake_case_names stay as they are.

1984\. A great year, written so it never starts a list.

\<!-- not a comment, the rest of the page stays text.

Stars kept as text: \*\*not bold\*\*, and a \`tick\` that is not code.

Tags and entities as typed: a \<br> tag and \&amp;, and backslashes kept: \\*stars\\\*.

Short code stays on one line: run `npm test`, then `npm run build && npm test -- --watch` when it wraps.

## Hard breaks

First line of an address, ending in a backslash\
Second line, ending in two spaces
Third line.

## Links over half-bold text

**b**[**old** t](https://example.com) is one link over half of a bold word.

A [plan link](https://example.com/plan), [[Plan]] and https://plan.example.com/plan: only the first is text that Replace changes.

## Replaced across formatting

Intro with Strong **words**, and **Fourth *slanted*** *here*: replacing or bolding half of a span splits it at the word.

## Formatting next to punctuation

file.**txt** · これは「**太字**」です · Opal(*beta*) · *every point it* makes, with

## Lists and headings that keep their marks

- A bullet whose text was replaced
- [ ] A task whose text was replaced
> A quote whose text was replaced
